Subject: [PATCH] wireguard: request outer UDP GRO before tunnel segmentation

Set GRO_ENABLED only on WireGuard-owned sockets. Standard UDP receive
still segments the aggregate before encap_rcv because WireGuard does not
accept UDP L4 GSO records. This amortizes the outer ingress stack while
preserving per-record authentication and ordering. No NIC-wide fraglist
setting changes.

---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireguard/socket.c b/drivers/net/wireguard/socket.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireguard/socket.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireguard/socket.c
@@ -343,6 +343,10 @@
 {
 	sock->sk->sk_allocation = GFP_ATOMIC;
 	sock->sk->sk_sndbuf = INT_MAX;
+	/* Aggregate outer UDP through GRO. The UDP tunnel receive path still
+	 * segments before invoking encap_rcv, so WireGuard receives one record.
+	 */
+	udp_set_bit(GRO_ENABLED, sock->sk);
 	sk_set_memalloc(sock->sk);
 }
 
